    "exact_excerpt": "B1 now binds the archived collector to historical commit e4abb172147e941b62483652b0ceabaae4317624, tree 016ebf3deeac88d6d7a782edf563f2291ebe17f5 and raw SHA256 f40c5d621454d0532141920724a3cfd57e240f4a3b061536162313daa676c254. The .py.raw fixture is data only and is never executed. All 25 original bridge test methods are unchanged; six added controls bring the component result to 31 passes. Separately, the full M4 Linux lane exposed a real closed-exec-gate cleanup race (root return code -15 instead of 125). C5 preserves the 14 original collector tests, adds two deterministic controls, and defers only SIGTERM for the unreleased root after confirmed gate closure; the original kill escalation and cleanup deadline remain. The exact final full-lane result is reported independently in the table above; these component facts do not grant hosted or system qualification.",
